    <briefdescription>
<para>Exact graph fallback policy and integration for tensor artifacts. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>ThemisDB EPIC 3 Implementation Team </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-07-03</para>
</simplesect>
This header defines policies for fallback to exact graph state when tensor artifacts are stale, invalid, or don&apos;t meet query accuracy requirements.</para>
<sect1 id="exact__graph__fallback_8h_1autotoc_md8_1s1"><sect2 id="exact__graph__fallback_8h_1autotoc_md8">
<title>Design Philosophy</title><para>The exact graph is always authoritative. Tensor artifacts are advisory-only. Fallback occurs when:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Artifact is not in ACTIVE state</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Advisory-only semantics mean artifact cannot guarantee correctness</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Query accuracy requirements cannot be met by artifact</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Residual is too high for the query&apos;s tolerance </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
